From: Tab5 Linux FPGA maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: physmap: preserve the size of direct ROM resources

The Tab5 boot shim exposes a 7 MiB read-only flash window as mtd-rom.
physmap currently rounds this down to the highest power of two, registering
only 4 MiB. A SquashFS image larger than 4 MiB then cannot mount even though
the flash partition and its mapped resource both cover the full image.

Use the resource size unchanged only when map_rom was explicitly selected
and no address-extension GPIOs are present. This includes the mtd-rom OF
binding without changing CFI/JEDEC probes, fallback ROM probing, or GPIO
bank-window calculations. The mapping never grows beyond its resource.

map_rom already accepts map->size directly, including a non-power-of-two
ROM resource. Its default erase size follows that size; the device remains
read-only and no flash erase/write path is added.

--- a/drivers/mtd/maps/physmap-core.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/maps/physmap-core.c
@@ -519,9 +519,14 @@
 			info->maps[i].phys = res->start;
 
 		info->win_order = fls64(resource_size(res)) - 1;
-		info->maps[i].size = BIT(info->win_order +
-					 (info->gpios ?
-					  info->gpios->ndescs : 0));
+		/* A plain ROM region need not have a power-of-two size. */
+		if (!info->gpios && info->probe_type &&
+		    !strcmp(info->probe_type, "map_rom"))
+			info->maps[i].size = resource_size(res);
+		else
+			info->maps[i].size = BIT(info->win_order +
+						 (info->gpios ?
+						  info->gpios->ndescs : 0));
 
 		info->maps[i].map_priv_1 = (unsigned long)dev;
 
